capability tls/read-write  the bytes of a TLS connection read and written
  heroes  io.read
  go      tls.Conn.Read, tls.Conn.Write
  rust    Read and Write of native_tls::TlsStream and rustls::StreamOwned, rustls::Connection::reader, rustls::Connection::writer
  python  ssl.SSLSocket.read, ssl.SSLSocket.write, ssl.SSLSocket.recv, ssl.SSLSocket.send, ssl.SSLSocket.sendall, ssl.SSLObject.read, ssl.SSLObject.write
  note    `io` reads and writes it, buffers it and splits its lines; nothing here does it twice (README § A6)

capability tls/roots  the authorities trusted: the system's own store, or only those given
  heroes  tls.Client
  go      tls.Config.RootCAs
  rust    native_tls::TlsConnectorBuilder::add_root_certificate, TlsConnectorBuilder::disable_built_in_roots, native_tls::Certificate::from_pem, Certificate::from_der, Certificate::stack_from_pem, rustls::RootCertStore, RootCertStore::add, RootCertStore::add_parsable_certificates, ClientConfig::with_root_certificates
  python  ssl.SSLContext.load_verify_locations, ssl.SSLContext.load_default_certs, ssl.SSLContext.set_default_verify_paths, ssl.get_default_verify_paths, ssl.DefaultVerifyPaths, ssl.SSLContext.cert_store_stats, ssl.SSLContext.get_ca_certs
  note    Roots given are the only ones trusted, as Go's `RootCAs` and Python's `cafile` make them; native-tls adds them to the system's unless `disable_built_in_roots`. Replacing is the stricter of the two, and pins a private authority

capability tls/identity  a server's certificate chain and private key read from PEM
  heroes  tls.Server
  go      tls.X509KeyPair, tls.LoadX509KeyPair, tls.Certificate, tls.Certificate.Leaf, tls.Certificate.PrivateKey
  rust    native_tls::Identity::from_pkcs8, rustls::pki_types::CertificateDer, rustls::pki_types::PrivateKeyDer
  python  ssl.SSLContext.load_cert_chain
  note    PKCS #8, PKCS #1 and SEC 1 keys, RSA and ECDSA on P-256, P-384 and P-521; an encrypted key is refused `invalid`, as Go refuses it, where Python asks for its password. Text, not a path: `fs.read_file` reads one

